## Overview

The AQ Fund Dashboard supports exploration of fine-particulate pollution and monitoring capacity across participating countries. Users can examine active monitors, awardee groups, reporting completeness, average PM₂.₅ concentrations, geographic patterns, monitoring gaps, and historical trends.

The current application combines:

- Ground-monitoring data for 2025–2026
- Satellite-derived PM₂.₅ estimates for 1998–2024
- Country, state, and district-level geographic views
- Monitoring-network and data-availability indicators
- Interactive charts, maps, drilldowns, and tables

## UI Components

The interface is organized into three primary UI components.

### GIS

The GIS component provides an interactive spatial view of air-quality monitoring data.

Key capabilities include:

- Country, state, and year filters
- Summary indicators for active monitors, awardee groups, average PM₂.₅, and data availability
- Ground-monitoring and satellite PM₂.₅ map modes
- State-level choropleth layers loaded by default
- District boundaries and monitor locations loaded on demand
- Interactive Leaflet tooltips, legends, popups, clustering, and fullscreen controls
- Searchable country, state, and district summary tables

### Monitoring Gaps

The Monitoring Gaps component highlights differences in pollution exposure and monitoring capacity.

It includes:

- Year selection for 2025 and 2026
- Country ranking by average PM₂.₅ concentration
- Active-monitor categories for comparing monitoring coverage
- Data-availability, awardee, and reporting-month details in chart tooltips
- Country-by-month PM₂.₅ heatmaps for identifying temporal and geographic gaps
- Reference to the WHO annual PM₂.₅ guideline within the priority visualization

### Trend Analysis

The Trend Analysis component presents annual and monthly PM₂.₅ patterns.

It supports:

- Country and year selection
- Annual PM₂.₅ trends combining satellite estimates for 1998–2024 with ground-monitoring averages for 2025–2026
- National PM₂.₅ standard reference lines where available
- Monthly ground-monitoring trends
- Optional state and district drilldowns
- Interactive Highcharts tooltips, legends, and validation states

## Core Indicators

| Indicator | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Active Monitors | Distinct ground monitors reporting data for the selected geography and year |
| Awardee Groups | Distinct awardee or monitoring-network groups represented in the selected records |
| Average PM₂.₅ | Mean fine-particle concentration across selected observations, reported in µg/m³ |
| Data Availability | Average percentage of expected observations reported by selected monitors |

